// Title: Suspicious File Created In PerfLogs
// Sigma ID: bbb7e38c-0b41-4a11-b306-d2a457b7ac2b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects suspicious file based on their extension being created in "C:\PerfLogs\". Note that this
//   directory mostly contains ".etl" files
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - Internal Research
//   - https://labs.withsecure.com/publications/fin7-target-veeam-servers
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_perflogs_susp_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath startswith "C:\\PerfLogs\\" and (FolderPath endswith ".7z" or FolderPath endswith ".bat" or FolderPath endswith ".bin" or FolderPath endswith ".chm" or FolderPath endswith ".dll" or FolderPath endswith ".exe" or FolderPath endswith ".hta" or FolderPath endswith ".lnk" or FolderPath endswith ".ps1" or FolderPath endswith ".psm1" or FolderPath endswith ".py" or FolderPath endswith ".scr" or FolderPath endswith ".sys" or FolderPath endswith ".vbe" or FolderPath endswith ".vbs" or FolderPath endswith ".zip")
